.TH FLUXLAND-KEYS 5 "2026-10-24" "fluxland 1.1.0" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
fluxland-keys \- key and mouse bindings (the Fluxbox keys file)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The keys file binds keys and mouse buttons to commands.
It is read the way Fluxbox reads its
.IR ~/.fluxbox/keys ,
so a Fluxbox keys file works unchanged; the commands are also used by
menu items and by
.BR fluxland-ctl (1).
.PP
The file is
.I ~/.config/fluxland/keys
(or
.I ~/.fluxbox/keys
when fluxland uses a Fluxbox configuration directory); the init file's
.B session.keyFile
names another.
.B fluxland \-\-check\-config
reports every line fluxland would not bind, and why.
.SH SYNTAX
Each line is one binding:
.PP
.RS 4
.RI [ mode\fB:\fP "] [" modifier " ...] " key " [" modifier " ... " key " ...] :" command
.RE
.PP
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
or
.B !
are ignored.
The words are not case sensitive.
.SH MODIFIERS
.TP
.B Shift
.TP
.BR Control " (or " Ctrl )
.TP
.BR Mod1 " (or " Alt )
The Alt key.
.TP
.B Mod4
The Super (Windows) key.
.TP
.BR Mod2 ", " Mod3 ", " Mod5
Mod5 is usually AltGr.
.TP
.B None
No modifier.
.PP
CapsLock and NumLock (Lock and Mod2) are left out when keys are
matched, as in Fluxbox: bindings work whichever of them is on.
.SH KEYS
A key is an XKB keysym name, such as
.BR Return ,
.BR space ,
.BR Tab ,
.BR F1 ,
.BR a ,
.BR 1 ,
.BR Left ,
.BR XF86AudioRaiseVolume ,
or a number that isn't a key name: a keycode, as
.BR xev (1)
shows it
.RB ( "176 :Exec amixer sset Master 1+" ).
A key is the key itself, whatever Shift does to it:
.B Mod1 Shift Tab
is Shift and the Tab key.
.SS Chains
Several keys before the command make a chain, pressed one after
another (within 5 seconds):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Mod4 x Mod4 t :Exec foot
.fi
.RE
.PP
Escape, or a key the chain doesn't continue with, ends it.
.B Arg
in a chain (not first) stands for whichever key comes there, for
.BR MarkWindow " and " GotoMarkedWindow :
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Mod4 m Arg :MarkWindow
Mod4 g Arg :GotoMarkedWindow
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mod4 m, then 1, marks the focused window as 1; Mod4 g, then 1, goes
back to it.
.SS Key modes
A line that starts with a mode name and a colon belongs to that key
mode; the others are the
.B default
mode.
.B KeyMode
.I name
switches to a mode; its end keys
.RB ( "None Escape"
unless given) go back to the default mode:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Mod4 v :KeyMode move Escape
move: h :MoveLeft 10
move: l :MoveRight 10
move: OnWindow Mouse1 :StartMoving
.fi
.RE
.PP
A mode has only its own bindings, mouse ones too.
.SH MOUSE BINDINGS
.RS 4
.RI [ context " ...] [" modifier " ...] [" \fBDouble\fP "] " event " :" command
.RE
.PP
The words can come in any order.
.SS Events
.TP
.BI Mouse N
The button is pressed.
.TP
.BI Click N
The button is pressed and released without moving.
.TP
.BI Move N
The pointer moves with the button held.
.TP
.BI "Double Mouse" N
A double click (fluxland also takes
.BI Double N\fR).
.PP
Lines can also bind these events, without a button:
.TP
.BR FocusIn ", " FocusOut
A window gets or loses the focus (always
.BR OnWindow ,
without modifiers), as in
.BR "FocusIn :Raise" .
.TP
.B ChangeWorkspace
Another workspace is shown (after its window has the focus).
.TP
.BR MouseOver ", " MouseOut
The pointer moves onto or off a window, or the toolbar or slit with
.BR OnToolbar " or " OnSlit ;
modifiers held count.
.PP
Buttons are numbered as in X: 1 left, 2 middle, 3 right, 4 and 5 the
wheel up and down, 6 and 7 the wheel left and right, 8 and 9 back and
forward.
A wheel binding takes the wheel's steps there (a touchpad keeps
scrolling).
A press a binding takes isn't passed on to the window.
.SS Contexts
.TP
.B OnDesktop
The desktop.
A binding with no context is also for the desktop only, as in Fluxbox.
.TP
.B OnWindow
A window's content.
.TP
.B OnTitlebar
A window's titlebar.
.TP
.B OnTab
A tab (the titlebar's label).
.TP
.BR OnWindowBorder ", " OnLeftGrip ", " OnRightGrip
The border and handle, and the handle's corners.
.TP
.BR OnWinButton ", " OnMinButton ", " OnMaxButton
A titlebar button: any, the minimize button, the maximize button.
These are
.BI Click N
bindings; they replace the button's own action.
.TP
.B OnToolbar
The toolbar.
.TP
.B OnSlit
The slit.
.PP
Several contexts can be given:
.BR "OnTitlebar OnTab Mouse2 :Lower" .
.SH CLIENT PATTERNS
Commands that choose windows take a pattern: terms in parentheses,
all of which must match, each
.BI ( property = regex )
or
.BI ( property != regex ).
The regex (POSIX extended) must match the whole value.
A bare word matches the name:
.B (xterm)
is
.BR (name=xterm) ;
a bare property, or
.BR [current] ,
matches what the focused window (or the current workspace) has:
.BR (workspace) ,
.BR (class=[current]) .
.TP
.BR name ", " class
X11 windows' WM_CLASS instance and class; a Wayland window's app_id.
.TP
.BR title ", " role ", " tag
The title; X11 WM_WINDOW_ROLE; xdg-toplevel-tag.
.TP
.BR workspace ", " workspacename ", " head ", " layer
Where the window is (workspaces count from 0 here).
.TP
.BR transient ", " maximized ", " maximizedhorizontal ", " maximizedvertical ", " minimized ", " fullscreen ", " shaded ", " stuck ", " focushidden ", " iconhidden ", " urgent
.B yes
or
.BR no .
.TP
.BI @ name
A window's text property (see SetXProp).
.PP
Window lists (NextWindow, GoToWindow...) also take
.BR {static} ,
creation order instead of focus order, and
.BR {groups} ,
one entry per tab group.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands act on a window: the one clicked for a mouse binding, each
window for ForEach, otherwise the focused one.
Numbers are workspaces, heads and tabs counting from 1; where noted, a
negative number counts from the end.
.SS Windows
.TP
.BR Close ", " Kill " (" KillWindow )
.TP
.BR Minimize " (" Iconify ", " MinimizeWindow "), " Maximize " (" MaximizeWindow "), " MaximizeHorizontal ", " MaximizeVertical ", " Fullscreen
.TP
.BR Shade " (" ShadeWindow "), " ShadeOn ", " ShadeOff ", " Stick " (" StickWindow )
.TP
.BR Raise ", " Lower ", " RaiseLayer " [\fIn\fP], " LowerLayer " [\fIn\fP]"
By n Fluxbox layers (2, one layer, by default).
.TP
.BI SetLayer " layer"
.BR Top ", " Normal ", " Bottom ", " Desktop ,
the other Fluxbox names, or a Fluxbox layer number (see
.BR fluxland-apps (5)).
.TP
.BI SetDecor " decoration\fR, " ToggleDecor
.BR NORMAL ", " NONE ", " BORDER ", " TAB ", " TINY ", " TOOL ,
or a Fluxbox decoration bitmask.
.TP
.BR SetAlpha " [\fIfocused\fP [\fIunfocused\fP]]"
Opacity 0\-255, or relative with
.B +
or
.BR \- ;
one value for both; none goes back to the init file's.
.TP
.BR Deiconify " [\fImode\fP [\fIdestination\fP]]"
The most recently iconified window of this workspace
.RB ( LastWorkspace ,
the default), of any
.RB ( Last ),
or all of them
.RB ( AllWorkspace ", " All ).
To the current workspace
.RB ( Current ,
the default), or its own:
.B OriginQuiet
leaves it there,
.B Origin
goes there too.
.SS Moving and resizing
.TP
.BR StartMoving ", " StartResizing " [\fIcorner\fP], " StartTabbing
Mouse moves, resizes and tab drags.
.TP
.BI MoveTo " x y \fR[\fIcorner\fP]"
Pixels or percent of the head,
.B *
to leave a coordinate, from a corner of the head
.RB ( TopLeft " by default, " Top ", " TopRight ", " Left ", " Center ,
.BR Right ", " BottomLeft ", " Bottom ", " BottomRight ).
.TP
.BI ResizeTo " width height"
The window's size with its decorations, pixels or percent of the head;
0 keeps one.
.TP
.BI Move " dx dy\fR, " MoveLeft " d\fR, " MoveRight " d\fR, " MoveUp " d\fR, " MoveDown " d"
.TP
.BI Resize " dw dh\fR, " ResizeHorizontal " dw\fR, " ResizeVertical " dh"
Pixels, or percent of the window's size.
.PP
Moving or resizing a maximized window un-maximizes it, unless
.B session.screen0.maxDisableMove
or
.B maxDisableResize
are set.
.B Move
and
.B Resize
without numbers start a mouse move or resize (fluxland).
.SS Focus
.TP
.BR NextWindow ", " PrevWindow " [{\fIoptions\fP}] [\fIpattern\fP]"
Cycle through the window list while the modifiers are held.
.TP
.BR NextGroup ", " PrevGroup " [\fIpattern\fP]"
.TP
.BI GoToWindow " N \fR[{\fIoptions\fP}] [\fIpattern\fP]"
The Nth window of the list (from the end when negative).
.TP
.BR Focus " [\fIpattern\fP], " Activate " [\fIpattern\fP]"
Focus the window, or the first matching the pattern.
.TP
.BR FocusLeft ", " FocusRight ", " FocusUp ", " FocusDown
.TP
.BR MarkWindow ", " GotoMarkedWindow
See
.B Arg
under Chains.
.TP
.BI SetFocusProtection " protection"
The window's
.B [FocusProtection]
(see
.BR fluxland-apps (5)):
.BR Gain ", " Refuse ", " Lock ", " Deny
or
.BR None ,
separated by commas.
.SS Workspaces
.TP
.BI Workspace " N"
(Negative from the end; out of range is the first or last.)
.TP
.BR NextWorkspace ", " PrevWorkspace " [\fIn\fP]"
n workspaces on, wrapping; 0 goes back to the workspace before.
.TP
.BR RightWorkspace ", " LeftWorkspace " [\fIn\fP]"
Without wrapping.
.TP
.BI SendToWorkspace " N\fR, " TakeToWorkspace " N"
Send the window there (Take goes with it).
.TP
.BR SendToNextWorkspace ", " SendToPrevWorkspace ", " TakeToNextWorkspace ", " TakeToPrevWorkspace " [\fIn\fP]"
.TP
.BR AddWorkspace ", " RemoveLastWorkspace ", " SetWorkspaceName " \fIname\fP"
.TP
.B SetWorkspaceNameDialog
A dialog to type the workspace's name in.
.TP
.BR SetHead " \fIN\fP, " SendToNextHead ", " SendToPrevHead " [\fIn\fP]"
.TP
.BR ShowDesktop ", " CloseAllWindows
.TP
.BR ArrangeWindows ", " ArrangeWindowsVertical ", " ArrangeWindowsHorizontal " [\fIpattern\fP]"
The shown windows of this workspace on the pointer's head (that match)
in a grid over it, as near square as can be, each cell taking the
window nearest it; shaded ones go down the sides.
Vertical lays them side by side, Horizontal one above another.
.TP
.BR ArrangeWindowsStackLeft ", " ArrangeWindowsStackRight ", " ArrangeWindowsStackTop ", " ArrangeWindowsStackBottom " [\fIpattern\fP]"
The focused window big on one half, the others in a grid on the half
named.
.TP
.BR Unclutter " [\fIpattern\fP]"
Those windows placed again where they overlap least.
.TP
.BR CascadeWindows " [\fIpattern\fP]"
One after another, a step down and right each.
.SS Tabs
.TP
.BI Tab " N"
The Nth tab (from the end when negative).
.TP
.BR NextTab ", " PrevTab ", " MoveTabLeft ", " MoveTabRight ", " DetachClient
.TP
.BR ActivateTab " [\fIN\fP]"
The tab under the pointer (or tab N).
.TP
.BR Attach " [\fIpattern\fP]"
Tab the windows matching the pattern together, into the most recently
focused of them.
.SS Menus
.TP
.BR RootMenu ", " WorkspaceMenu ", " WindowMenu ", " ClientMenu ", " WindowList ", " HideMenus
.TP
.BI CustomMenu " path"
.SS Commands
.TP
.BI Exec " command\fR (" ExecCommand ", " Execute )
Run a command with
.B $SHELL
(or
.BR /bin/sh ).
.TP
.BI MacroCmd " {command} {command} ..."
.TP
.BI ToggleCmd " {command} {command} ..."
The next command each time.
.TP
.BI Delay " {command} \fR[\fImicroseconds\fP]"
Run it once the binding stops repeating (200 by default).
.TP
.BI If " {condition} {then} \fR[{\fIelse\fP}]" "\fR (" Cond )
.TP
.BI ForEach " {command} \fR[{\fIcondition\fP}]" "\fR (" Map )
For each window (that meets the condition).
.TP
.BI KeyMode " mode \fR[\fIend keys\fP]"
.TP
.BI BindKey " binding"
Add a binding (a key mode's or a mouse one too) and write it at the
end of the keys file, so it stays.
.TP
.BI SetEnv " name value\fR, " Export " name=value"
.TP
.BI SetStyle " path\fR, " ReloadStyle
A style file, or a directory with theme.cfg or style.cfg.
.TP
.B CommandDialog
A dialog to type a command in, as on a key binding: Return runs it,
Escape closes it, Tab finishes a command's name.
.TP
.BI SetTitle " title\fR, " SetTitleDialog
The window's title (or a dialog to type it in), kept whatever the
program calls itself after.
.TP
.BI SetResourceValue " resource value\fR, " SetResourceValueDialog
Set a resource of the init file (saved there) and read the
configuration again, as
.B SetResourceValue session.screen0.toolbar.visible false
does.
.TP
.BI SetXProp " name=value"
Give the window a text property, which
.BI (@ name = value )
patterns match (an X window's own X property).
.TP
.BI ClientPatternTest " pattern"
The windows matching the pattern, as the IPC reply's
.B result
.RB ( "fluxland-ctl action ClientPatternTest (class=foot)" ):
.BI 0x id
and the title, a line each;
.B 0
for none.
.TP
.BI RelabelButton " button.NAME label"
A toolbar button's label, until the configuration is read again.
.TP
.B SaveRC
Nothing to do: fluxland saves a setting when it changes.
.TP
.BR Reconfigure " (" Reconfig ", " Restart )
Read the configuration again.
fluxland can't restart under its windows, so Restart does this too.
.TP
.BR Exit " (" Quit )
.SS Conditions
.TP
.BI Matches " pattern"
The window matches.
.TP
.BI Some " condition\fR, " Every " condition"
Some or every window meets it.
.TP
.BI Not " condition\fR, " And " {c} {c} ...\fR, " Or " ...\fR, " Xor " ..."
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
OnDesktop Mouse3 :RootMenu
OnDesktop Mouse4 :NextWorkspace
OnTitlebar Double Mouse1 :Shade
OnTitlebar Move1 :StartMoving
OnWindow Mod1 Mouse1 :MacroCmd {Raise} {Focus} {StartMoving}
OnMaxButton Click3 :Fullscreen

Mod1 Tab :NextWindow {groups} (workspace=[current])
Mod4 Return :Exec foot
Mod4 Left :MoveTo 0 0 TopLeft
Mod4 h :MacroCmd {ResizeTo 50% 100%} {MoveTo 0 0}
Mod4 e :If {Some Matches (class=firefox)} {Focus (class=firefox)} {Exec firefox}
Control Mod1 Right :NextWorkspace
Control Mod1 BackSpace :NextWorkspace 0
.fi
.RE
.SH COMPATIBILITY
fluxland 1.x bound a mouse binding with no context everywhere, and
.B OnWindow
covered the decorations too; both now follow Fluxbox: write
.BR "OnWindow Mod1 Mouse1" .
Buttons 4 and 5 are the wheel (they were the side buttons, now 8
and 9).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fluxland (1),
.BR fluxland-apps (5),
.BR fluxland-init (5),
.BR fluxland-menu (5),
.BR fluxland-ctl (1),
.BR regex (7)
